{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a troop shall troop upon him.</b> All of them are from the root גְּדוּד, and so Menachem arranged it. And if you would say: there is no גְּדוּד without two dalets — one may say: גְּדוּד as a noun requires two dalets, for so is the way of a two-letter word to double its final letter, and its root is only two letters. And so: ״כַּצִּפּוֹר לָנוּד״ (Proverbs 26), ״מִגִּזְרַת שָׂבַעְתִּי נְדֻדִים״ (Job 7), ״שָׁם נָפַל שָׁדוּד״ (Judges 5), ״מִגִּזְרַת יָשׁוּד צָהֳרָיִם״ (Psalms 91) — likewise יָגֻד, יְגוּדֶנּוּ, and גְּדוּד are from one root. And when it speaks in the binyan of יִפְעֹל it is not doubled, such as יָגוּד, יָנוּד, יָרוּם, יָשׁוּד, יָשׁוּב. But when it is hitpa'el or hif'il of others, it is doubled, such as יִתְגּוֹדֵד, יִתְרוֹמֵם, יִתְבּוֹלֵל, יִתְעוֹדֵד; and in the hif'il: ״יָתוֹם וְאַלְמָנָה יְעוֹדֵד״ (Psalms 146), ״לְשׁוֹבֵב יַעֲקֹב אֵלָיו״ (Isaiah 49), ״מְשֹׁבֵב נְתִיבוֹת״ (ibid. 58). The יְגוּדֶנּוּ spoken of here is not a form where others act upon it, but rather like יָגוּד הֵימֶנּוּ — as in ״בָּנַי יְצָאֻנִי״ (Jeremiah 10) — they went out from me. <b>Gad, a troop shall troop upon him</b>: troops shall go forth from him to cross the Jordan with their brothers for the battle, every armed man, until the land was conquered." "<b>And he shall troop at the heel.</b> All his troops shall return on their heels to the inheritance they took across the Jordan, and not a single man of them shall be missing." "<b>At the heel.</b> On their routes and on the highways they traveled, they shall return — as in ״וְעִקְּבוֹתֶיךָ לֹא נֹדָעוּ״ (Psalms 77), and likewise ״בְּעִקְבֵי הַצֹּאן״ (Song of Songs 1); בִּלְשׁוֹן לַעַז טרצי״אם."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "the second dibbur ha-matchil repeats the lemma of verse 49:19a to introduce the peshat interpretation after the grammatical discussion", 2 "the la'az טרצי״אם likely represents Old French (a)tres/derriere, 'behind/heels'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:19.854283219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}